## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic React Native native bridge concepts, event flow, and cross-platform APIs in a small, tangible task.

## Key Concepts
- React Native bridging and NativeEventEmitter
- Platform APIs: NWPathMonitor vs ConnectivityManager
- Promise-based native calls and lifecycle of listeners

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal JS wrapper
import { NativeModules, NativeEventEmitter } from 'react-native';
const { OfflineStatus } = NativeModules;
const emitter = new NativeEventEmitter(OfflineStatus);
export const useOfflineStatus = () => {
  const [offline, setOffline] = useState(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    const sub = emitter.addListener('offlineChanged', setOffline);
    OfflineStatus.isOffline().then(setOffline);
    return () => sub.remove();
  }, []);
  return offline;
}
```

